1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,563
We are SELADEVS UTHM.

2
00:00:01,563 --> 00:00:07,031
SHIFTATLAS helps Malaysian graduates choose a credible next learning step as AI changes work.

3
00:00:07,031 --> 00:00:12,109
Our prototype connects reviewed skills with evidence, explainable role coverage and affordable learning.

4
00:00:13,538 --> 00:00:15,224
Aina is our fictional graduate.

5
00:00:15,224 --> 00:00:20,622
She can use spreadsheets, but cannot tell whether SQL, Python or another skill should come next.

6
00:00:20,622 --> 00:00:26,019
A useful result explains the trade-off and gives her an ordered plan that fits her time.

7
00:00:29,009 --> 00:00:32,351
The same profile connects all six modules.

8
00:00:32,351 --> 00:00:34,739
Dated signals inform role coverage.

9
00:00:34,739 --> 00:00:37,126
Visible gaps become learning steps.

10
00:00:37,126 --> 00:00:40,946
SDG pathways add purpose, while scenarios expose uncertainty.

11
00:00:40,946 --> 00:00:45,720
The interface offers both 3D exploration and equivalent text controls.

12
00:00:47,382 --> 00:00:49,725
Resume parsing stays on the device.

13
00:00:49,725 --> 00:00:57,143
Users can load a synthetic PDF, DOCX or text file and inspect the original excerpt behind each detected mention.

14
00:00:57,143 --> 00:01:00,266
They review the evidence and choose their level.

15
00:01:00,266 --> 00:01:04,170
The avatar reflects those self-assessments, without inferring personality or employability.

16
00:01:05,755 --> 00:01:09,094
An updatable arXiv feed supplies dated research titles.

17
00:01:09,094 --> 00:01:15,354
An explicit experiment counts skill-topic mentions and adjusts existing weights by at most twenty-five percent.

18
00:01:15,354 --> 00:01:20,780
In the current synthetic example, analyst coverage changes from sixty-nine to seventy percent.

19
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:23,283
This demonstrates a working data-to-score loop.

20
00:01:23,283 --> 00:01:26,622
Research attention does not establish Malaysian hiring demand.

21
00:01:27,995 --> 00:01:31,926
Each role score exposes current level, target and weight.

22
00:01:31,926 --> 00:01:37,603
O*NET supplies the six occupation references, while the project authors the numerical rubric.

23
00:01:37,603 --> 00:01:40,661
Users can inspect every contribution and gap.

24
00:01:40,661 --> 00:01:45,465
The percentage describes rubric coverage, with Malaysian transferability still requiring validation.

25
00:01:47,335 --> 00:01:53,983
Learning Islands places foundations before dependent activities and estimates a sequence using skill gaps and weekly time.

26
00:01:53,983 --> 00:01:56,330
Real provider resources support each activity.

27
00:01:56,330 --> 00:01:59,458
Learners can track steps and export the plan.

28
00:01:59,458 --> 00:02:03,368
Completion records activity and does not automatically certify a skill.

29
00:02:04,741 --> 00:02:09,626
The Malaysia atlas uses actual DOSM state boundaries and quarterly state observations.

30
00:02:09,626 --> 00:02:13,696
We preserve that resolution and avoid city or individual inferences.

31
00:02:13,696 --> 00:02:18,581
Every role and required skill also connects to a specific SDG target.

32
00:02:18,581 --> 00:02:23,873
The app explains intended contributions across all seventeen goals, without claiming measured outcomes.

33
00:02:25,047 --> 00:02:28,728
The simulator compares a supported transition with accelerated adoption.

34
00:02:28,728 --> 00:02:32,408
Users change the year and inspect every chosen coefficient.

35
00:02:32,408 --> 00:02:36,906
These hypothetical indices illustrate how adoption and learning support could interact.

36
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:43,449
We assign no scenario probability and make no forecast of jobs lost or an individualâ€™s employment.

37
00:02:45,354 --> 00:02:48,463
Atlas Quest adds a playable low-poly island.

38
00:02:48,463 --> 00:02:52,460
Five checkpoints reinforce evidence review, geographical resolution and uncertainty.

39
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:56,901
Unique badges, outfits and companions personalise the saved explorer passport.

40
00:02:56,901 --> 00:02:59,122
The rewards track exploration only.

41
00:02:59,122 --> 00:03:04,008
A learner study is still needed to establish an engagement benefit.

42
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:12,593
Our Career Council gives one AI model four specialist roles: profile reviewer, career explorer, learning planner and critic.

43
00:03:12,593 --> 00:03:15,289
Each stage builds on the previous suggestions.

44
00:03:15,289 --> 00:03:18,369
The critic challenges the reasoning and highlights trade-offs.

45
00:03:18,369 --> 00:03:26,842
Our gateway brings the stages together around the same trusted catalogue, helping learners compare choices while keeping their original skill scores intact.

46
00:03:27,901 --> 00:03:31,021
We designed the Council around source-linked choices.

47
00:03:31,021 --> 00:03:38,599
Our gateway checks the response structure, recognised roles and courses, and exact quotations from the fictional profile.

48
00:03:38,599 --> 00:03:43,501
It restores learning prerequisites and keeps API keys on the server.

49
00:03:43,501 --> 00:03:48,404
Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 supplies the four review roles; E5 separately provides semantic retrieval.

50
00:03:48,404 --> 00:03:51,524
Learners retain control over the final choice.

51
00:03:53,042 --> 00:03:59,911
We built and ran our E5 worker on RunPod using a PRO six thousand M I G, twenty-four gigabyte GPU.

52
00:03:59,911 --> 00:04:09,869
Our recorded fictional query compared two role descriptions and returned CUDA results in three point four five two seconds, after eleven point six two six seconds in the queue.

53
00:04:09,869 --> 00:04:14,677
We also passed fifty-five application tests, eighteen offline worker checks and the production build.

54
00:04:14,677 --> 00:04:18,110
Our submission includes the actual request history and completion receipt.

55
00:04:19,151 --> 00:04:22,012
Our next phase brings SHIFTATLAS to ten learners.

56
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:28,449
We aim for twenty percent less median planning time and eighty percent correctly explaining their score and uncertainty.

57
00:04:28,449 --> 00:04:35,244
We built the project with OpenAI Codex and GPT-five-point-one Sol, alongside coding assistance from Qoder and Cortex Code, CoCo.

58
00:04:35,244 --> 00:04:41,324
Our goal is clear: help learners choose a next step they can understand, afford and act on.

59
00:04:42,358 --> 00:04:45,284
These are actual recorded views of the prototype.

60
00:04:45,284 --> 00:04:47,843
The fictional sample produces eight skill dimensions.

61
00:04:47,843 --> 00:04:51,499
The evidence layer shows the original sentence for data literacy.

62
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:56,984
A reviewer can deselect a mention, then accept it at a minimum level of one.

63
00:04:56,984 --> 00:04:58,812
The self-assessment controls remain editable.

64
00:04:58,812 --> 00:05:00,640
No real CV is needed.

65
00:05:04,599 --> 00:05:09,150
Future Skills City displays dated public references and a refreshable research snapshot.

66
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:14,458
The comparison table shows the baseline and experimental scores before the toggle is applied.

67
00:05:14,458 --> 00:05:19,767
For the analyst sample, the research emphasis changes coverage from sixty-nine to seventy percent.

68
00:05:19,767 --> 00:05:22,421
The small change is visible and explainable.

69
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:29,080
Career Bridges ranks six reference roles.

70
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:34,683
The analyst table exposes the current level, target, weight and score contribution for each skill.

71
00:05:34,683 --> 00:05:36,550
These are authored rubric values.

72
00:05:36,550 --> 00:05:42,526
A higher percentage means more rubric coverage, and does not mean a higher probability of employment.

73
00:05:47,146 --> 00:05:52,211
The learning route puts prerequisite foundations before dependent practice and shows estimated weeks.

74
00:05:52,211 --> 00:05:55,328
The time comes from the selected weekly availability.

75
00:05:55,328 --> 00:06:00,782
Each activity links to a real provider resource, and the plan can be exported.

76
00:06:00,782 --> 00:06:03,509
Completion flags record activity without certifying proficiency.

77
00:06:06,486 --> 00:06:09,410
Atlas Quest offers a second way to engage.

78
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:11,603
The explorer walks to a checkpoint.

79
00:06:11,603 --> 00:06:15,623
A correct answer unlocks its badge and one hundred exploration points.

80
00:06:15,623 --> 00:06:20,009
The passport saves the outfit, companion and equipped title in this browser.

81
00:06:20,009 --> 00:06:23,298
All five checks are also available through text controls.

82
00:06:27,759 --> 00:06:31,555
The source map preserves Malaysian state boundaries and state-level statistics.

83
00:06:31,555 --> 00:06:36,110
The Node gateway connects optional semantic retrieval and four Council review stages.

84
00:06:36,110 --> 00:06:39,527
The public repository contains the code and Apache licence.

85
00:06:39,527 --> 00:06:42,943
Methods, tools and sources are documented alongside the code.

86
00:06:42,943 --> 00:06:48,637
The result is a sourced next step that a learner can inspect, change and revisit.
